Sval: offer Always allow as its own button in the camera prompt

The camera and microphone prompt answered with Allow or Block, and made
either one permanent through a "Remember for all cameras and microphones"
checkbox, so Always allow was a checkbox plus a button and easy to miss.
Where the prompt can grant for good (a secure page, outside private
browsing, a camera or microphone), WebRTCParent's prompt offers Always
allow as a third answer in place of the checkbox. It runs the main
action as the checked checkbox did.

PopupNotifications lists every secondary action past the first in the
secondary button's chevron menu. options.actionButtons shows each of them
as a button of its own (SvalPromptButtons), and their clicks take the same
focus and security-delay checks as the other two buttons.

